    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0534" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg406"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 293.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kasson to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 4, 1885</date>.
                        (Received April 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 223.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have heretofore communicated to the
                    Department several statements of military cases of German-American citizens
                    which presented hardships of such a nature as to prove the necessity of another
                    effort to improve the provisions of the German-American naturalization treaty of
                    1868.</p>
                <p>Herewith I now inclose the complaint of Ernst F. Heitmüller, which presents an
                    instance of such grave injustice that it became my duty to request of the German
                    Government some action beyond its ordinary course, and in special condemnation
                    of the local officials who committed the wrong. The case is stated in my note to
                    the foreign office, copy of <pb facs="0535" n="407" xml:id="pg407"/> which is
                    herewith inclosed, together with an acknowledgment received from that office,
                    and translation of the same.</p>
                <p>The response of the foreign office may be delayed beyond my term of service; and
                    the case may tend to influence such instructions on the general subject as you
                    shall desire to give to my successor. I therefore forward it without awaiting
                    the reply.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN A. KASSON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d293-a1.xml" xpointer="d293-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d293-a2.xml" xpointer="d293-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
